    "updated_at": "2016-12-21T21:18:51Z",
    "body": "Thank you for tagging! I think you have a point! _But I think the web is changing_: There are so many applications out there not reloading the page anymore. Some features just can't be integrated with that existing security model. I think it would be a huge benefit to be able to address a user directly from a portion of a script (of course, you can do that already today, but showing a label outside the browsing area just provides credibility on another level). Targetting this feature request will be the first step to provide isolation which is _**visible**_ by users.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
