    "created_at": "2016-12-21T21:31:03Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-12-21T21:47:06Z",
    "body": "I don't think that such \"_labels_\" would degrade security. It would be orthogonal to existing ideas: The most important part of the idea is that a user can \"**_immediately see_**\" which pages have access to the information he/she/it is providing. Iframes are within the browsing area and only people who want to examine the page structure will realise that \"some input X\" is located within an iframe. External labels just provide that information fragment transparently to the user.\r\n\"Secure input elements\" as I call them just need their \"_capturing ability_\", because such a \"_**trust**_\" must be credible on technical aspects as well.\r\n(bugs exist; and attackers use them; so even if the developer hasn't intended some foreign script on the page, at least the user would see foreign effects - iff secure inputs were well-established)",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
