    "created_at": "2016-12-22T23:21:36Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-12-22T23:21:36Z",
    "body": "In particular, a concrete attack against this would be for the 3rd party script to just... remove the input, and put in an identical one without the secure attribute.  Invisible to the user (it wouldn't show the banner, but *most* sites won't show the banner, so it won't be that noticeable), and it lets them harvest all they want.\r\n\r\nOr the 3rd party script can replace some of the functions in the document, so that when the main-page script tries to do something with the contents, it exposes the value accidentally.\r\n\r\nThere are myriad other attacks like this. This is why, as Domenic says, we don't try to protect against scripts included into the document. They can do too much; you've already lost all security guarantees at that point.  All we'd be doing is providing a false sense of security, and slowing down very naive attackers.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
